{"id": "REL-GH-02", "criterion": "A package that targets `github-release` gets `gh release create <tag> --repo <owner/repo> --verify-tag --draft`, adding `--prerelease` for prerelease versions. After all its assets upload, the release is published with `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false`."}

{"id": "REL-GH-03", "criterion": "Release notes are the body of the package CHANGELOG section for the version, passed with `--notes-file`. With no changelog configured, a missing or unreadable file, or a missing or empty section, Callisto passes `--generate-notes` and prints `notes: using generated notes (<reason>) for <package>` to stderr."}

{"id": "REL-GH-04", "criterion": "Each `[[release.artifact]]` becomes one upload named `asset-name` on the product package's GitHub release, tagged with the product's own tag and prerelease flag regardless of the asset owner package's version. An artifact whose `package` is not in the release fails with E179, and a `product-package` that is missing or does not target `github-release` fails with E197. When an artifact's owner package is selected but the product package is not, Callisto warns on stderr, records a `product-artifact-owner-without-product` diagnostic (surfaced in `--format json`; see REL-CMD-04), and derives no slot for that asset.", "is_error_case": true}

{"id": "REL-GH-06", "criterion": "Before any effect, `release execute` fails with E139 when an artifact's bytes differ from the manifest. It fails with E140 unless `gh attestation verify` passes with the configured `--repo`, `--signer-workflow <repo>/.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml`, `--signer-digest` set to the orchestration revision, `--source-digest` and `--deny-self-hosted-runners`.", "is_error_case": true}

{"id": "REL-ERR-03", "criterion": "A `[release]` section fails config loading with E197 when it has no `[[release.artifact]]`, an unqualified `product-package` or artifact `package`, an unsafe `target` or `asset-name`, or a duplicate `asset-name`. It also fails for a `[release.profiles.<name>]` other than `production`, or a `production` forge-repository that conflicts with the top-level key.", "is_error_case": true}

